WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.365
Download models from an approved source and verify the intended revision before spending time loading them.

00:00:07.365 --> 00:00:16.414
A persistent cache or reusable disk can reduce repeated transfers, but it continues to generate cost and must be protected.

00:00:16.414 --> 00:00:25.883
For disposable instances, consider whether a clean automated download is safer and cheaper than retaining a large cache between infrequent sessions.

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:32.828
Quantization reduces memory demand and may allow a model to run on a smaller rental.

00:00:32.828 --> 00:00:37.668
Evaluate the quality and speed tradeoff with the actual task.

00:00:37.668 --> 00:00:46.296
Configure an inference server with explicit model, context, batch, and GPU settings, then expose it through an authenticated API.

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:53.240
Keep the endpoint private while testing, and apply request limits and timeouts before sharing it.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:58.080
Concurrency controls simultaneous sequences and increases cache and compute pressure.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:03.341
Batching can improve total throughput but may delay an individual request.

00:01:03.341 --> 00:01:11.127
Measure time to first output, prompt-processing speed, generation speed, queue time, errors, and completed work per hour.

00:01:11.127 --> 00:01:15.546
Include network latency between the client and rental region.

00:01:15.546 --> 00:01:21.649
A fast benchmark inside the instance may not represent the user's end-to-end experience.

00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:26.489
Test real prompts, context lengths, documents, images, and failure cases.

00:01:26.489 --> 00:01:32.591
Watch VRAM, GPU utilization, CPU, RAM, disk, and network while the test runs.

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:42.482
If the accelerator remains underused, identify whether tokenization, data transfer, queueing, or an unsupported backend is responsible before renting a larger device.

00:01:42.482 --> 00:01:49.847
The goal is the lowest-cost configuration that completes the workload reliably, not the largest GPU available.
